es/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:238:  \"src\": \"framed lower region with black background and colored interior marker pixels\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:239:  \"transform\": \"copy the palette row; select the unique most frequent marker color, clear the lower region to black, recolor the outer frame, and draw that color's bbox border\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:287:overlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:rectangle, operation:count, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:294:Move colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:297:- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:303:Key insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:308:  \"src\": \"sprite s in the left area whose color appears on the right frame\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:309:  \"dst\": \"center at positions d in the right frame\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:322:overlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:rectangle, operation:reflect, operation:repair_anomaly, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:329:Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by replacing singleton markers, filling short orthogonal gaps, and redirecting yellow-marked arms to the edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:333:- Line colors form one-cell-thick horizontal/vertical stroke fragments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:335:- Red singleton markers are missing line cells; yellow singleton markers are directional controls next to a line endpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:338:- Assign every marker to the nearest visible line color in row/column line-of-sight, preferring an endpoint supported along that same axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:343:Key insight: The singleton markers identify which sparse stroke fragments belong together; after they are colored, the intended lines are the axis-aligned gaps between facing endpoints, with yellow controls flipping one arm to the marked side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:348:  \"src\": \"one-cell-thick colored line network with singleton red/yellow marker pixels\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:349:  \"transform\": \"replace each marker by its assigned line color, fill facing horizontal/vertical gaps, and use yellow controls to erase the old arm and paint the same color from the endpoint through the marker to the grid edge\",\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/17/codegen_prompts/1.md:350:  \"notes\": \"crossings prefer yellow-control rays; otherwise original-vs-filled crossings use the more fragmented repaired line, and marker-bracketed filled gaps beat unmarked pure fills\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:38:Push every colored object touching maroon markers straight outward until it reaches the grid edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:42:- Maroon pixels are fixed markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:43:- Every other foreground 4-connected object touches the marker pixels on exactly one cardinal side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:48:- Keep the maroon marker pixels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:65:- Yellow stripes paint only within the segment's span.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:74:Complete each partial marker mask by stamping the matching multicolor sprite over it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:79:- A target mask may contain only one marker pixel or several same-alignment marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:86:- Stamp the whole sprite at those translations; if a non-marker sprite color occurs as\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:87:  a single source pixel, consume that source-only marker back to background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:97:Infer the background, rotate the whole input 90 degrees counterclockwise, and stack two framed copies vertically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:101:- One rare marker color appears in exactly two pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:102:- The background is the unique non-marker color whose removal leaves exactly two 4-connected foreground objects, each with one marker pixel and one body color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:107:- Create a blue one-pixel frame around two vertical copies of the rotated grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:166:- If the blue edge is vertical, rotate each rectangle 90° CCW.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:175:Extract the top-left or top-right 2x2 corner crop selected by the top edge clue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:185:  a left or right edge and take the 2x2 top-corner crop on that side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:218:- bg = background. A hollow NxN square (hub) with bg corners/interior and four differently-colored edges (top, bottom, left, right).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:223:- Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:246:- The original foreground colors are only markers; the output color depends on each marker's ordinal position in the dominant scan direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:349:Assemble scattered rectangular pieces into a rectangle at an L-marker corner.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:353:- 3-pixel L-marker (2x2 minus one cell) tags the corner; the gap is the corner cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:365:Reveal the rectangular patch hidden by the solid marker using the grid's reflection symmetries.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:368:- A square colored pattern with one solid rectangular marker color occluding a patch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:369:- The visible pattern has horizontal and vertical reflection symmetry on a large lower/right strip.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:374:- Infer the reflected strip start as the smallest row/column offset whose lower/right strips are mirror-consistent, ignoring marker pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:375:- For each marker pixel, copy the unique non-marker value in its horizontal/vertical reflection orbit; if that orbit is entirely hidden in the outer strip, use the transposed top/left-strip counterpart.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:378:The marker is not part of the pattern; it covers a missing rectangle whose cells are still determined by the visible mirror or transpose copies elsewhere in the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:384:Shift each row's dominant middle-color run left until its right edge aligns with the leftmost original right edge, moving displaced left-side pixels after the run.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:392:- Find the minimum right edge column among the middle-color runs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:393:- In each row, keep the run width and the trailing right-side color count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:394:- Place the middle-color run so its right edge is at that minimum column, unless the run is too wide, in which case start it at column 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:398:The varying row prefixes are movable padding; the stable feature is the leftmost right boundary of the middle-color shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:423:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:424:   - **不建议使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算 / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/prompt.md:427:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/des.md:2:- `description`：将每个模板框内的缺损像素修复为其同行/同列中的对称位置颜色，同时根据缺损数量在框外绘制计数标记。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/des.md:6:  - 网格中有若干个由 Maroon 一像素厚矩形边框围成的区域，每个区域内部有一个本应具有左右对称性的多色图案。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/des.md:7:  - 每个图案中有 1-3 个像素被替换为背景色（缺损），破坏了对称性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/17/des.md:10:  - 对每个框内的图案，找到其垂直对称轴。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/see